    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40805" root="هب" body-key="h">
    
      R. Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْهَبْتُهُ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبَبْتُ بِهِ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْهَبَ</span>, inf.
n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْهَبَةٌ</span>, <i>He was quick,</i> or <i>swift.</i> (K.) See
also 1. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْهَبَ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْهَبَةٌ</span>, <i>It</i> (the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَرَاب</span>, or
mirage,) <i>glistened,</i> or <i>shone;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَرَقْرَقَ</span>; (K;)
i. e., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَمَعَ</span>. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْهَبَ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْهَبَةٌ</span>, <i>He
urged,</i> or <i>checked,</i> [app. the former,] <i>with his
voice;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَجَرَ</span>; (K;) by saying <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْ</span>. (R, as
cited by MF,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْ هَبْ</span>: [so I understand from
the TA, where it is said <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">والفعل منه هَبْ هَبْ</span>; for
which it is evident that we should read <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَٱسْمُ الفِعْلِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">منه الخ</span>; meaning “ its ” (imperative) verbal a
&amp;c.:] accord. to some, used specially with reference to a horse: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هاب</span> [in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هيب</span>]. (TA.)
You also say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْهَبَ بِهِ</span>. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْهَبَ</span>, inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَبْهَبَةٌ</span>, <i>He slaughtered</i> [a beast]. (K.)

